###  https://purl.org/cbam/validity_date
properties:validity_date rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                         rdfs:label "Validity Date"@en ;
                         rdfs:comment "The date from which a CN code entry is valid, reflecting the annual updates to the Combined Nomenclature published by the European Commission in the Official Journal of the European Union. CN codes may be added, removed, or restructured with each yearly revision, so this date identifies the applicable nomenclature version."@en .


###  https://purl.org/cbam/CN/cn10_code
vocabulary:cn10_code rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                     rdfs:label "CN10 Code"@en ;
                     rdfs:comment "The 10-digit CN code, extending the 8-digit Combined Nomenclature code with 2 additional digits used in the EU TARIC system for statistical, tariff, and trade policy purposes. This is the most granular level of the EU tariff classification."@en ;
                     rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                     rdfs:domain vocabulary:CN .


###  https://purl.org/cbam/CN/cn6_code
vocabulary:cn6_code rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                    rdfs:label "CN6 Code (HS Subheading)"@en ;
                    rdfs:comment "The 6-digit Harmonized System (HS) subheading code, which forms the common international basis of the CN classification as defined by the World Customs Organization (WCO). The first 2 digits identify the chapter, digits 3-4 the heading, and digits 5-6 the subheading. This level is shared across all WCO member countries."@en ;
                    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                    rdfs:domain vocabulary:CN .


###  https://purl.org/cbam/CN/cn8_code
vocabulary:cn8_code rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                    rdfs:label "CN8 Code (Combined Nomenclature)"@en ;
                    rdfs:comment "The 8-digit Combined Nomenclature code, composed of the 6-digit HS subheading code plus 2 EU-specific subdivision digits. This is the standard level used for EU customs tariff declarations, Intrastat reporting, and external trade statistics. It corresponds directly to the CN code published in the Official Journal of the European Union."@en ;
                    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                    rdfs:domain vocabulary:CN .


###  https://purl.org/cbam/CN/cn_code
vocabulary:cn_code rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                   rdfs:label "CN Code (Formatted)"@en ;
                   rdfs:comment "The formatted Combined Nomenclature code as officially published in the EU Official Journal, typically presented with spaces separating digit groups (e.g., '1001 11 00'). This human-readable format is used in legal texts, tariff schedules, and customs documentation. For structural groupings (sections, chapters, headings) that do not have a tradeable CN8 code, this value may be absent or set to the grouping identifier (e.g., 'I', '10')."@en ;
                   rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                   rdfs:domain vocabulary:CN .


###  https://purl.org/cbam/CN/code
vocabulary:code rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                rdfs:label "Internal CN Entry Code"@en ;
                rdfs:comment "The full internal code identifier for a CN entry, combining the 10-digit CN code with a 2-digit positional suffix that distinguishes the role of the line in the tariff hierarchy. Lines ending in '0010' or '0090' are structural groupings (parent headings with no tradeable commodity code), while lines ending in '0080' represent actual tradeable commodity codes for which customs declarations can be made."@en ;
                rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                rdfs:domain vocabulary:CN .


###  https://purl.org/cbam/CN/hs6_code
vocabulary:hs6_code rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                    rdfs:label "HS6 Code (Harmonized System)"@en ;
                    rdfs:comment "The 6-digit Harmonized Commodity Description and Coding System (HS) subheading code maintained by the World Customs Organization (WCO). This code is the internationally harmonised basis used by over 200 countries for customs tariff classification and trade statistics. In the CN, this corresponds to the first 6 digits of the CN8 code and is identical to cn6_code."@en ;
                    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                    rdfs:domain vocabulary:CN .


###  https://purl.org/cbam/CN/hs8_code
vocabulary:hs8_code rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                    rdfs:label "HS8 Code (CN Tariff Subheading)"@en ;
                    rdfs:comment "The 8-digit tariff subheading code equivalent to the CN8 code, used in the context of the EU Combined Nomenclature for customs duty purposes, Intrastat declarations, and statistical reporting. It extends the 6-digit HS subheading with 2 EU-specific digits and is functionally equivalent to the cn8_code property."@en ;
                    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
                    rdfs:domain vocabulary:CN .


